  "worked_solution": "The local truncation error (LTE) is the error made in a *single step* of a numerical method, when the step begins from an *exact value*. The LTE of a numerical method at step $n$ from $x$ with exact value ${y}_{\\text{exact}}(x)$ to ${x}_{\\text{new}}=x+\u0394x$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\u03c4}_{n} & ={y}_{\\text{exact}}({x}_{\\text{new}})-{y}_{\\text{new}} \\\\  & ={y}_{\\text{exact}}({x}_{\\text{new}})-({y}_{\\text{exact}}(x)+\u0394y).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe find the LTE at each step, rounding to three decimal places in each case:\n\n- After the first step, we have ${x}_{\\text{new}}=0.29$ and ${y}_{\\text{new}}=0.995.$ So, the LTE of the first step is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\u03c4}_{1} & ={y}_{\\text{exact}}(0.29)-0.995 \\\\  & =(0.29)^{3}+1-0.995 \\\\  & \u22480.029.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- After the second step, we have ${x}_{\\text{new}}=0.58$ and ${y}_{\\text{new}}=1.225.$ So, the LTE of the second step is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\u03c4}_{2} & ={y}_{\\text{exact}}(0.58)-1.225 \\\\  & =(0.58)^{3}+1-1.225 \\\\  & \u2248-0.030.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- After the third step, we have ${x}_{\\text{new}}=0.87$ and ${y}_{\\text{new}}=1.625.$ So, the LTE of the third step is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\u03c4}_{3} & ={y}_{\\text{exact}}(0.87)-1.625 \\\\  & =(0.87)^{3}+1-1.625 \\\\  & \u22480.034.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the completed table is as given below.\n\n| $n$ | $x$ | $y$ | ${\u03c4}_{n}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $0$ | $1.000$ | $0$ |\n| $1$ | $0.29$ | $0.995$ | $0.029$ |\n| $2$ | $0.58$ | $1.225$ | $-0.030$ |\n| $3$ | $0.87$ | $1.625$ | $0.034$ |",
